  parent owns the shared unit metadata. No Lean or TeX build was run.

  <section|Exact source correspondence><label|exact-source-correspondence>

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.common> and
    <verbatim|common_price>, in <verbatim|LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/Enrolled.lean>,
    form the finite active-coordinate common row from <verbatim|fullRow> and
    transfer the bed's exponential width using <verbatim|fullRow_width>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.enrolled>,
    same file, identifies the repeated forest <verbatim|treeMatrix> exactly
    with the restriction of <verbatim|common.acts>; the identification uses
    the zero-offset repeated forest and <verbatim|link> active-coordinate
    equivalence.

    <item><verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.cofinal_prices>,
    same file, transports a positive gap from large periods to every period.
    <verbatim|Universal.modulo> gives the quotient homomorphism;
    <verbatim|Universal.law> intertwines convolution under pullback;
    <verbatim|dot_push> counts every fiber by <verbatim|card ker>. The
    manuscript gives this finite reindexing proof rather than treating
    \Pcofinal\Q as a gap theorem.

    <item><verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.reserve>,
    <verbatim|treeFare_pos>, and <verbatim|earned>, in
    <verbatim|Covers.lean>, use the tree gap at threshold <verbatim|100 *
    macroR P + 3>, <verbatim|common_price>, and
    <verbatim|FreeResolvent.strip_resolvent>. The source gap is
    <verbatim|min(a, K.penalty)/(1 + beta + gamma)>, with beta and gamma
    exactly the curl and probe coefficients of the finite block estimate.
    <verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.tree_gap> in <verbatim|Flat.lean> proves this
    from the finite block curl/probe bound and bed floor. The manuscript
    cross-references the completed derivation in the canonical
    <verbatim|sec:path-attachment-producer>, including its
    site/axis/plaquette cardinalities and edge-comparison constant; it does
    not attribute the proof to <verbatim|sector-gram>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.Universal.law>, <verbatim|.inverses>,
    <verbatim|.folding>, and <verbatim|.publish>, in
    <verbatim|Push/FREE_RESOLVENT/Fold.lean>, provide translation-compatible
    period folding and the single cover inverse row. <verbatim|publish> uses
    factorial periods, coefficientwise compact extraction, the uniform
    exponential majorant, and dominated convergence. It does not use
    Fourier-symbol inversion. <verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.strip_resolvent> in
    <verbatim|Metric.lean> supplies its inverse-row exponential bound from
    the common row width and finite-period gap.

    <item><verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.rootMeter>,
    <verbatim|meter_width>, <verbatim|meter_reads>, and
    <verbatim|onePlateau>, in <verbatim|Covers.lean>, compose the same
    inverse with the rooted path rows and identify its restriction, at every
    admissible native step of coarse side at least 3, with <verbatim|plane *
    treeInverse * plane.transpose>. The positive strip width and row constant
    are selected before the bed and work uniformly over beds satisfying the
    fixed strip/floor bounds, as in <verbatim|earned>.
    <verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.TellerFold.cutHead>
    supplies the exact finite tree conditional curvature formula. The
    separate parent proof <verbatim|sec:actual-reader-tree-covariance>
    supplies the finite curl-through and conditional covariance algebra; this
    unit invokes, and does not duplicate, that proof. The rooted measurement
    row maps asked-coordinate vectors to curvature coordinates (rows
    <verbatim|dial>, columns <verbatim|Asked>).

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.WeightedGaussianMarginal45C.Issue.Cut.Figure>,
    <verbatim|.summon>, and <verbatim|.Figure.joints>, in
    <verbatim|Issue/Cut/Cells.lean>, symmetrize the cover representative by
    the real fixed-point operation. The output covariance matrices are
    symmetric, so this leaves every admissible tree period unchanged.
    <verbatim|Figure.joints> gives the entrywise cut error <verbatim|cheque>.
    The manuscript then defines the finite-range comparator to equal the
    exact covariance on base pairs within radius <verbatim|H_x> and zero
    outside; the error is zero on retained pairs and controlled by
    <verbatim|Figure.joints> plus <verbatim|enough_room> on omitted pairs.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.WeightedGaussianMarginal45C.Issue.Cut.ShapeCut>,
    <verbatim|.ShapeCut.draw>, <verbatim|cut_bounds>, <verbatim|order_exp>,
    and <verbatim|enough_room>, in <verbatim|Issue/Cut/Scissors.lean>, retain
    every coarse-cell cover displacement through the natural quotient
    <verbatim|radiusB/10000>, bound the omitted strip by
    <verbatim|exp(-s*leastHem)>, restrict retained support to the natural
    quotient <verbatim|radiusB/8>, and make cut entries zero beyond that
    coarse-base separation. <verbatim|YM.Pressure.radiusB> in
    <verbatim|Pressure/Seeds.lean> is <verbatim|ceil((log x)^2)>. Transpose
    symmetry must reverse displacement; the manuscript uses <verbatim|(a,b,z)
    -\<gtr\> (b,a,-z)>. The internal row labels carry intra-block residues
    and colors; spatial support uses the <verbatim|splitCo> parent-base
    coordinate.

    <item><verbatim|YM.Extra.IterationNoLoss.psi_strip> in
    <verbatim|Extra/ITERATION_NO_LOSS/Columns.lean> gives the inherited cover
    bound <verbatim|psiPrice(\<Omega\>,\<Omega\>')/L^2>; its proof composes
    the fine dual-diagonal row, moving tower row, and coarse diagonal row.
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.sufficient_rows> in
    <verbatim|AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Leading.lean> specializes
    this to <verbatim|psiBudget(M')/L^2> on the selected same history.
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.WeightedGaussianMarginal45C.Issue.Cut.psiBudget>
    and <verbatim|.contour_uses> in <verbatim|Issue/Cut/Cells.lean> give
    <verbatim|psiBudget(M') = \|TypeFace2\|^2 (M')^3> and the exact movement
    cheque <verbatim|cheque(TypeFace2,s,psiBudget(M')/L^2,x)>. Thus the
    <verbatim|L^-2> is an incoming tower strip factor, not an installation
    gain.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Paying>,
    <verbatim|.confers>, and <verbatim|.telescope>, in
    <verbatim|AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Epoch.lean>, are the
    same-history consumer. Under a constant consecutive blocking clock,
    <verbatim|telescope> combines the paid movement error with the paid
    cut-row cheque and uses <verbatim|enough_room> and the exact same-bed
    <verbatim|Figure.transfer>. This draft proves the concrete cut and its
    error implications but leaves production of those payments to the
    selected schedule.
  </enumerate>

  <section|What is proved here versus retained><label|what-is-proved-here-versus-retained>

  The period-folding lemma is newly reorganized from the exact quotient-map
  calculation: both the quadratic form and norm scale by the same positive
  kernel cardinality. The common inverse explanation follows
  <verbatim|Universal.publish> and <verbatim|Metric.strip_resolvent>, with
  the centered factorial-period extraction and all-period folding steps
  stated explicitly. Symmetric displacement cut-tail and support conclusions
  are proved directly from the strip bound and the natural quotient radii.
  The finite-range covariance comparator is exact on retained base pairs and
  differs only on the omitted tail. The tree-slice covariance identification
  is cross-referenced to the existing finite proof rather than rederived.

  The following are not proved in this unit and remain explicit inputs: the
  selected bed's exponential row bound; the all-large-period coercivity/floor
  receipt and its upstream physical construction; the chosen scale's movement
  and turn payments; consecutive-level clock plateau; path/capital bounds;
  and the upstream funding of these estimates. Thus the proposition is a
  same-history local covariance theorem conditional on actual quantified
  receipts, not a completed public construction result.

